      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-30T18:22:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is the accepted migration path for these sorts of printf() %s changes? Many of the things that we print are trivial compile-time const char* (albeit hidden in a different compilation unit), or come from std::string(foo).c_str() or SkString(foo).c_str().\n\nAre we expected to be migrating to std::format or blanket suppress this warning in our log macros?",
      "parentUuid": "d1e218c2_3b223bfb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 307,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 309,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "d12456fa64a3099a840ffbf9ac34eb65b28cec94",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e4112e3a_a6acb935",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawContext.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 309,
      "author": {
        "id": 4764846
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-30T19:59:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To fix this we can take two approaches:\n\n1- Rewrite the logic so it doesn\u0027t trigger the -Wunsafe-buffer-usage warning; maybe we could implement a std::string_view or std::format.\n\n2- If it is decided that we don\u0027t want to migrate this code, we can change the SK_UNSAFE_TODO macro to SK_UNSAFE_BUFFERS with a safety comment explaining why the approach is safe even if that part of the code triggers the warning. Part of the explanation could be something like what you described. I can take on follow-up CLs cleaning up this code and migrating it into SK_UNSAFE_BUFFERS so it no longer is considered technical debt.",
      "parentUuid": "7e97d1c1_316bad70",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 307,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 309,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "d12456fa64a3099a840ffbf9ac34eb65b28cec94",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a00f5d27_a3ea5c00",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/DrawContext.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 309,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-01T13:56:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For now can we update the SKIA_LOG and SKDEBUGFAILF, etc. macros to automatically include SK_UNSAFE_TODO so that we aren\u0027t polluting all of the log sites with their own SK_UNSAFE_TODOs?\n\nTalking with other leads, we need to consolidate our string representations from SkString, const char*, std::string, and std::string_view down to just std::string and std::string_view. At that point we can update our format strings to use string_view, or the compiler will be able to see that the %s maps to a std::string().c_str() call (which I believe it is able to detect as safe).",
      "parentUuid": "e4112e3a_a6acb935",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 307,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 309,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "d12456fa64a3099a840ffbf9ac34eb65b28cec94",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ccaf1352_f4817bb3",
