      "writtenOn": "2026-10-01T15:33:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sounds like a good plan!\n\n**String literals**\nClang consider `\"%s\", \"foo\"`to be safe.\n\n**std::string**: \nClang understand `\"%s\", str.c_str()` is safe. It has dedicated logic for -WUnsafe-buffer-usage.\n\n**std::string_view**: it\u0027s not guaranteed to be null-terminated, so with printf it needs to populate the size in the format: `\"%.*s\", static_cast\u003cint\u003e(sv.size()), sv.data()`. Clang also has dedicated logici to consider this safe. However, I feel the code to be a bit ugly.\n\nIf Abseil or C++20 \u003cprint\u003e/\u003cformat\u003e is possible in Skia someday, then they both natively understand C++ std::string view and it would become more readable.",
      "parentUuid": "a00f5d27_a3ea5c00",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 307,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 309,
        "endChar": 47
